<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Jonesborough, Tennessee</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1779">1779</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Jonesborough is a town in north-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tennessee">Tennessee</a>, founded in 1779 by North Carolina as the seat of Washington County and the oldest town in Tennessee. In 1784 delegates of the western counties met there and declared the State of Franklin, which made it its first seat of government. Its preserved historic centre now hosts the National Storytelling Festival.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/jonesborough-tennessee.jpg" alt="Jonesborough, Tennessee" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Brian Stansberry · CC BY 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Washington-county-courthouse-tn1.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
